Gear Patrol reported six hundred forty-seven horsepower

56
00:02:01,404 --> 00:02:04,796
and five hundred fifty pound-feet of torque,

57
00:02:04,796 --> 00:02:07,416
a top speed of two hundred sixteen

58
00:02:07,416 --> 00:02:08,572
miles per hour,

59
00:02:08,572 --> 00:02:10,885
and zero to sixty in two point

60
00:02:10,885 --> 00:02:11,887
nine seconds.

61
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:15,175
Wikipedia says power rose to six hundred

62
00:02:15,175 --> 00:02:17,895
sixty horsepower for twenty twenty.

63
00:02:18,245 --> 00:02:20,938
The V6 was chosen for a reason.

64
00:02:21,118 --> 00:02:23,954
Gear Patrol said the engine's slim packaging

65
00:02:23,954 --> 00:02:26,661
allowed the designers to build Ford's most

66
00:02:26,661 --> 00:02:28,595
aerodynamically efficient car.

67
00:02:28,775 --> 00:02:29,704
Look at the body.

68
00:02:29,884 --> 00:02:32,387
Between the cabin and the rear wheels,

69
00:02:32,387 --> 00:02:34,890
there are huge open channels where air

70
00:02:34,890 --> 00:02:36,339
flows through the car.

71
00:02:36,519 --> 00:02:39,057
That shape was only possible because the

72
00:02:39,057 --> 00:02:40,199
engine was narrow.

73
00:02:40,550 --> 00:02:43,688
The chassis is a carbon fiber monocoque,

74
00:02:43,688 --> 00:02:46,826
Wikipedia says, and Gear Patrol listed a

75
00:02:46,826 --> 00:02:50,356
dry weight of about three thousand fifty-four

76
00:02:50,356 --> 00:02:50,906
pounds.

77
00:02:51,086 --> 00:02:53,208
There is an active rear wing,

78
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:54,526
and in Track mode,

79
00:02:54,526 --> 00:02:57,087
which can only be selected when the

80
00:02:57,087 --> 00:02:58,185
car is stopped,

81
00:02:58,185 --> 00:03:00,601
the GT drops about two inches and

82
00:03:00,601 --> 00:03:02,870
its spoiler rises about a foot.

83
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:05,514
Gear Patrol listed a starting price of

84
00:03:05,514 --> 00:03:08,049
about four hundred fifty thousand dollars.

85
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,414
That is the car.

86
00:03:09,594 --> 00:03:11,101
Now, the first secret,

87
00:03:11,101 --> 00:03:13,843
which starts years before anyone saw it.

88
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:15,632
Secret number one.

89
00:03:15,812 --> 00:03:17,646
The Ford GT was born out of

90
00:03:17,646 --> 00:03:19,005
a cancelled Mustang.

91
00:03:19,185 --> 00:03:21,810
Jalopnik reported that Raj Nair,

92
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:25,092
then Ford's head of product development,

93
00:03:25,092 --> 00:03:27,882
had backed a racing Mustang for Le

94
00:03:27,882 --> 00:03:30,999
Mans, a program called Project Silver,

95
00:03:30,999 --> 00:03:33,953
named after the Lone Ranger's horse.

96
00:03:34,133 --> 00:03:36,188
It would even have had a carbon

97
00:03:36,188 --> 00:03:37,581
fiber passenger cell.

98
00:03:37,931 --> 00:03:40,369
But Project Silver was cancelled.

99
00:03:40,549 --> 00:03:43,181
Jalopnik, citing the Auto Extremist,

100
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:45,155
said it ground to a halt at

101
00:03:45,155 --> 00:03:47,494
the final go or no-go meeting in

102
00:03:47,494 --> 00:03:48,957
Mark Fields' office,

103
00:03:48,957 --> 00:03:51,954
because of cost and reluctance among some

104
00:03:51,954 --> 00:03:54,806
regional executives to pay their share.

105
00:03:54,986 --> 00:03:56,820
The racing Mustang was dead.

106
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:59,364
So Nair did something unusual.

107
00:03:59,544 --> 00:04:02,605
Jalopnik reported that he started a new

108
00:04:02,605 --> 00:04:04,018
program in secret,

109
00:04:04,018 --> 00:04:06,294
without his bosses' approval,

110
00:04:06,294 --> 00:04:09,512
in a basement warehouse at Ford's Product

111
00:04:09,512 --> 00:04:11,945
Development Center in Dearborn,

112
00:04:11,945 --> 00:04:12,652
Michigan.

113
00:04:12,832 --> 00:04:15,386
The team called it Project Phoenix,

114
00:04:15,386 --> 00:04:17,940
the bird that rises from the ashes.

115
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:20,159
And the secrecy was extreme.

116
00:04:20,339 --> 00:04:23,767
Motoring Research reported that the studio sat

117
00:04:23,767 --> 00:04:26,674
in a basement at Ford's Dearborn design

118
00:04:26,674 --> 00:04:30,252
center, while colleagues upstairs worked on cars

119
00:04:30,252 --> 00:04:32,413
like the Edge and the Fusion.

120
00:04:32,593 --> 00:04:34,948
The door to the studio was disguised

121
00:04:34,948 --> 00:04:36,257
as a broom cupboard,

122
00:04:36,257 --> 00:04:39,135
and designer Chris Svensson unlocked it with

123
00:04:39,135 --> 00:04:40,116
a physical key.

124
00:04:40,296 --> 00:04:42,293
He called it old school.

125
00:04:42,644 --> 00:04:44,647
Svensson also said that,

126
00:04:44,647 --> 00:04:47,986
fortunately, no one really asked what he

127
00:04:47,986 --> 00:04:49,238
was working on.

128
00:04:49,418 --> 00:04:52,292
Wikipedia quotes him saying that only a

129
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:55,313
handful of about twelve people had access

130
00:04:55,313 --> 00:04:56,860
to the design studio.

131
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,172
One of the most important Fords in

132
00:04:59,172 --> 00:05:01,554
decades was designed by a dozen people

133
00:05:01,554 --> 00:05:03,309
behind a fake cupboard door.

134
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:05,122
Here is the twist.

135
00:05:05,302 --> 00:05:08,415
Motoring Research said the performance team was

136
00:05:08,415 --> 00:05:10,004
involved from the start,

137
00:05:10,004 --> 00:05:12,454
while the accountants were kept away.

138
00:05:12,634 --> 00:05:14,616
That is why the design changed so

139
00:05:14,616 --> 00:05:16,718
little from the early clay model to

140
00:05:16,718 --> 00:05:17,859
the production car.

141
00:05:18,039 --> 00:05:19,638
In most car projects,

142
00:05:19,638 --> 00:05:21,847
the budget shapes the design.

143
00:05:22,027 --> 00:05:24,209
Here, the design came first.

144
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,835
And the reveal was a form of

145
00:05:26,835 --> 00:05:27,485
revenge.

146
00:05:27,665 --> 00:05:30,661
Jalopnik reported that Nair later took each

147
00:05:30,661 --> 00:05:33,865
executive who had rejected Project Silver down

148
00:05:33,865 --> 00:05:36,024
to the secret room to show them

149
00:05:36,024 --> 00:05:36,582
the car.

150
00:05:36,762 --> 00:05:39,363
The project that had been killed came

151
00:05:39,363 --> 00:05:41,401
back as something far bigger,

152
00:05:41,401 --> 00:05:43,932
a carbon fiber supercar built to win

153
00:05:43,932 --> 00:05:44,494
Le Mans.

154
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:47,293
Nair later told this story in public.

155
00:05:47,473 --> 00:05:50,781
Jalopnik reported that he described it at

156
00:05:50,781 --> 00:05:52,960
the S A E World Congress in

157
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,945
Detroit, saying the GT had risen from

158
00:05:55,945 --> 00:05:58,607
the ashes of the Mustang project.

159
00:05:58,787 --> 00:06:00,916
It is rare for a senior car

160
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:03,597
executive to admit that one of the

161
00:06:03,597 --> 00:06:06,752
company's most famous cars started as an

162
00:06:06,752 --> 00:06:08,644
unapproved side project.

163
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:10,166
Why Le Mans?

164
00:06:10,346 --> 00:06:11,774
Because of history.

165
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:13,680
In nineteen sixty-six,

166
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:16,190
Ford's G T forty finished first,

167
00:06:16,190 --> 00:06:19,484
second, and third at the twenty-four hours

168
00:06:19,484 --> 00:06:20,347
of Le Mans,

169
00:06:20,347 --> 00:06:24,033
ending Ferrari's run of six straight victories,

170
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:25,759
Petrolicious reported.

171
00:06:25,939 --> 00:06:28,471
The new GT was designed to return

172
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:30,466
exactly fifty years later.

173
00:06:30,817 --> 00:06:33,269
And that rivalry started with a failed

174
00:06:33,269 --> 00:06:33,591
deal.

175
00:06:33,771 --> 00:06:37,572
Petrolicious reported that in nineteen sixty-three,

176
00:06:37,572 --> 00:06:39,510
Ford tried to buy Ferrari,

177
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:43,385
spending several million dollars on negotiations and

178
00:06:43,385 --> 00:06:43,907
audits.

179
00:06:44,087 --> 00:06:47,104
The deal collapsed when Ford refused to

180
00:06:47,104 --> 00:06:49,966
give Enzo Ferrari full control of his

181
00:06:49,966 --> 00:06:51,204
racing programs.

182
00:06:51,384 --> 00:06:53,988
Ford decided to beat Ferrari on the

183
00:06:53,988 --> 00:06:55,029
track instead.

184
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:58,410
Even the nineteen sixty-six win had drama.

185
00:06:58,590 --> 00:07:01,435
Wikipedia says Ken Miles was leading when

186
00:07:01,435 --> 00:07:03,447
Ford told him to slow down so

187
00:07:03,447 --> 00:07:05,737
three of its cars could cross the

188
00:07:05,737 --> 00:07:07,541
line together for a photo.

189
00:07:07,721 --> 00:07:10,761
Because Bruce McLaren's car had started further

190
00:07:10,761 --> 00:07:12,766
back and covered more distance,

191
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:15,354
McLaren and Chris Amon were declared the

192
00:07:15,354 --> 00:07:15,871
winners.

193
00:07:16,051 --> 00:07:17,770
Miles finished second.

194
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:18,956
And it worked.

195
00:07:19,136 --> 00:07:22,625
Wikipedia says that in twenty sixteen,

196
00:07:22,625 --> 00:07:25,655
a Ford Chip Ganassi Racing GT won

197
00:07:25,655 --> 00:07:27,216
the L M G T E Pro

198
00:07:27,216 --> 00:07:28,777
class at Le Mans,

199
00:07:28,777 --> 00:07:33,276
fifty years after the nineteen sixty-six victory.

200
00:07:33,456 --> 00:07:35,823
A car designed in a basement behind

201
00:07:35,823 --> 00:07:38,055
a fake broom cupboard had won the

202
00:07:38,055 --> 00:07:40,422
world's most famous endurance race,

203
00:07:40,422 --> 00:07:41,301
in its class,

204
00:07:41,301 --> 00:07:42,721
at its first attempt.

205
00:07:43,072 --> 00:07:45,510
The original G T forty did not

206
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:47,379
stop at one win either.

207
00:07:47,559 --> 00:07:51,152
Petrolicious reported that in nineteen sixty-seven,

208
00:07:51,152 --> 00:07:53,266
the G T forty Mark four became

209
00:07:53,266 --> 00:07:56,788
the first entirely American-designed and built car

210
00:07:56,788 --> 00:07:57,845
to win Le Mans,

211
00:07:57,845 --> 00:08:00,311
and that Ford won again in nineteen

212
00:08:00,311 --> 00:08:02,847
sixty-eight and nineteen sixty-nine,

213
00:08:02,847 --> 00:08:05,102
four Le Mans victories in a row.

214
00:08:05,282 --> 00:08:07,743
The new GT carried that legacy on

215
00:08:07,743 --> 00:08:08,788
its shoulders.

216
00:08:09,138 --> 00:08:11,355
It is a story Hollywood would love.

217
00:08:11,535 --> 00:08:12,504
And in fact,

218
00:08:12,504 --> 00:08:13,956
three years later,

219
00:08:13,956 --> 00:08:16,539
Hollywood told the original one.

220
00:08:16,719 --> 00:08:20,141
The twenty nineteen film Ford versus Ferrari

221
00:08:20,141 --> 00:08:23,329
dramatized the nineteen sixties G T forty

222
00:08:23,329 --> 00:08:26,596
program, with Matt Damon as Carroll Shelby

223
00:08:26,596 --> 00:08:29,629
and Christian Bale as driver Ken Miles,

224
00:08:29,629 --> 00:08:31,417
according to Wikipedia.

225
00:08:31,768 --> 00:08:33,207
Secret number two.

226
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:35,330
The Ford GT race car was so

227
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:38,352
effective that it changed one of Porsche's

228
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:39,935
most famous race cars.

229
00:08:40,115 --> 00:08:43,074
Gear Patrol reported that after the GT's

230
00:08:43,074 --> 00:08:46,625
success, Porsche re-engineered its nine eleven R

231
00:08:46,625 --> 00:08:48,401
S R Le Mans race car for

232
00:08:48,401 --> 00:08:52,026
twenty seventeen, moving its flat-six engine from

233
00:08:52,026 --> 00:08:54,023
the very back of the car to

234
00:08:54,023 --> 00:08:54,837
the middle.

235
00:08:55,187 --> 00:08:57,439
Think about how big that is.

236
00:08:57,619 --> 00:08:59,790
The nine eleven has always had its

237
00:08:59,790 --> 00:09:01,578
engine behind the rear axle.

238
00:09:01,758 --> 00:09:03,697
It is the car's identity.

239
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:07,460
For decades, Porsche engineered around that layout

240
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:09,252
instead of abandoning it.

241
00:09:09,432 --> 00:09:12,396
Gear Patrol said Porsche moved the engine

242
00:09:12,396 --> 00:09:15,794
to improve aerodynamic efficiency and close the

243
00:09:15,794 --> 00:09:18,035
gap with the Ford on the track.

244
00:09:18,386 --> 00:09:20,711
Why would the engine position matter so

245
00:09:20,711 --> 00:09:21,009
much?

246
00:09:21,189 --> 00:09:23,052
A race car makes much of its

247
00:09:23,052 --> 00:09:25,779
downforce with a large diffuser under the

248
00:09:25,779 --> 00:09:26,112
rear.

249
00:09:26,292 --> 00:09:28,461
With the engine hanging at the very

250
00:09:28,461 --> 00:09:30,506
back, there is less room for that

251
00:09:30,506 --> 00:09:31,064
diffuser.

252
00:09:31,244 --> 00:09:34,374
Moving the engine forward freed up space

253
00:09:34,374 --> 00:09:36,644
at the rear for aerodynamics,

254
00:09:36,644 --> 00:09:39,148
exactly where the Ford GT was so

255
00:09:39,148 --> 00:09:39,696
strong.

256
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:42,428
So the Ford GT's narrow V6 and

257
00:09:42,428 --> 00:09:45,049
its air channels did not only win

258
00:09:45,049 --> 00:09:45,526
races.

259
00:09:45,706 --> 00:09:47,800
They pushed a rival to rethink a

260
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:50,090
design that had defined it for half

261
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:50,744
a century.

262
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:53,146
That is the kind of impact few

263
00:09:53,146 --> 00:09:54,256
cars ever have.

264
00:09:54,607 --> 00:09:57,195
There is another detail inside the car

265
00:09:57,195 --> 00:09:58,693
that surprises people.

266
00:09:58,873 --> 00:10:00,325
The seats do not move.

267
00:10:00,505 --> 00:10:03,337
Gear Patrol reported that the bucket seats

268
00:10:03,337 --> 00:10:05,900
are fixed directly to the carbon fiber

269
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:06,170
tub.

270
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,841
Instead, the pedal box and the steering

271
00:10:08,841 --> 00:10:10,692
wheel move to fit the driver.

272
00:10:10,872 --> 00:10:13,329
The pedal box adjusts with a nylon

273
00:10:13,329 --> 00:10:14,123
pull strap.

274
00:10:14,473 --> 00:10:16,133
This is race car thinking.

275
00:10:16,313 --> 00:10:18,919
Fixing the seats to the structure saves

276
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:20,856
weight, keeps the driver low,

277
00:10:20,856 --> 00:10:22,860
and makes the seat part of the

278
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:23,395
chassis.

279
00:10:23,575 --> 00:10:25,663
It is unusual in a road car,

280
00:10:25,663 --> 00:10:27,900
and it tells you what the Ford

281
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:28,869
GT really is.

282
00:10:29,049 --> 00:10:31,766
A Le Mans car with license plates.

